# Line endings: LF in the repository and in the working tree, on every OS.
#
# This is not cosmetic here.  The committed generated kernels are compared
# byte-for-byte by the CI freshness gate (tools/regenerate.py --check), and
# that script normalizes its own output to LF.  A checkout that materializes
# them with CRLF would have to diff equal to LF bytes for the gate to mean
# anything; the rule below removes the question.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never mangle binaries.  *.exe matters: the vendored codegen tool
# (tools/yacas/bin/yacas.exe) is a PE32+ executable committed to this tree,
# and a line-ending filter applied to it is a corrupt maintainer tool.
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
